        "id": 1003966
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-06-17T01:00:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The wildcard is also useful for the policy writer, to define how they want to handle namespaces unknown to SELinux policy. It should be up to the policy writer to choose to allow or deny access to them. By failing to support a wildcard, you end up with a situation where the policy writer can\u0027t make that determination. The policy writer is ultimately the entity which determines the access control rules, not the code itself.",
      "parentUuid": "c9e6eb46_857dbb1b",
